\b MbewuSmart - How to Run the App\b0\par
\par
\b 1. Prerequisites\b0\par
- Flutter SDK installed and working\par
- Android Studio installed with Android SDK\par
- Android emulator created (for example Pixel)\par
- Project folder: C:\\Users\\Praise Simba Phiri\\Documents\\GitHub\\mbewusmart\par
\par
\b 2. Open Terminal in Project Folder\b0\par
Use PowerShell and run commands from the project root.\par
\par
\b 3. Verify Flutter Path\b0\par
Run:\par
where flutter\par
flutter --version\par
\par
If you see objective_c or path-space errors, use:\par
C:\\dev\\flutter\\bin\\flutter.bat\par
\par
\b 4. Start Emulator\b0\par
flutter emulators\par
flutter emulators --launch <emulator_id>\par
flutter devices\par
\par
\b 5. Run App on Emulator\b0\par
flutter run -d emulator-5554\par
\par
Path workaround:\par
C:\\dev\\flutter\\bin\\flutter.bat run -d emulator-5554\par
\par
\b 6. Hot Reload / Hot Restart\b0\par
While app is running:\par
- r = Hot Reload\par
- R = Hot Restart\par
- q = Quit\par
\par
\b 7. Common Fixes\b0\par
A) No supported devices connected\par
- Start emulator in Android Studio Device Manager\par
- Run flutter devices again\par
\par
B) Error: 'C:\\Users\\Praise' is not recognized\par
- Usually Flutter path-with-spaces issue\par
- Run with: C:\\dev\\flutter\\bin\\flutter.bat run -d emulator-5554\par
- Ensure user PATH prioritizes C:\\dev\\flutter\\bin\par
\par
C) AI not responding\par
- Confirm GEMINI_API_KEY exists in .env\par
- Check network/DNS access to generativelanguage.googleapis.com\par
\par
\b 8. Helpful Commands\b0\par
flutter clean\par
flutter pub get\par
flutter doctor -v\par
flutter devices\par
\par
\b 9. Stop Emulator\b0\par
adb -s emulator-5554 emu kill\par
